  "goodToKnow": "Die Tinte is ink: die Tintenpatrone (ink cartridge), der Tintenstrahldrucker (inkjet printer). German primary school children traditionally learn to write with a Füller (fountain pen) and blue ink, using a Tintenkiller to erase. Idiom: in der Tinte sitzen means to be in a fix. Der Tintenfisch (ink fish) is a squid or octopus. Plural: die Tinten."
